  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop in pcre2test on a negative repeat count\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-41409.patch: reject a zero or negative repeat\n       value in a subject line in src/pcre2test.c.\n     - CVE-2022-41409\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write in the DFA matcher workspace\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86145.patch: check that a reused workspace\n       block is large enough and clamp a new block to the remaining heap\n       limit without overflow in more_workspace() in src/pcre2_dfa_match.c.\n     - CVE-2026-86145\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: invalid free after JIT fast path matching\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-89161.patch: free a previously copied subject\n       and clear PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT in pcre2_jit_match() in\n       src/pcre2_jit_match.c.\n     - CVE-2026-89161\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write on large JIT stack allocations\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-103111.patch: grow the JIT stack enough to\n       cover allocations larger than half the growth rate in\n       src/pcre2_jit_compile.c.\n     - CVE-2026-103111",
